    },
    {
      "id": "Ads_98r6Wr5VjBbI-ADCj",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 288.82571263380146,
      "y": 262.0294323219756,
      "width": 1366.1990966796875,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bKx",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 635488324,
      "version": 403,
      "versionNonce": 981822332,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731911679519,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Before starting with react as the frontend part In our Mern \nstack it's good to know what React.js actually is :\n\nReact.js is one the most popular frontend library among Vue.js\nAngular.js but what makes React so good is it is simple to understand\nand it gives us the ability to build single page application\n\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Before starting with react as the frontend part In our Mern \nstack it's good to know what React.js actually is :\n\nReact.js is one the most popular frontend library among Vue.js\nAngular.js but what makes React so good is it is simple to understand\nand it gives us the ability to build single page application\n\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "oRutre_JyLb5YNQUxddCS",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 294.79599626470383,
      "y": 692.3489622371992,
      "width": 1385.9990234375,
      "height": 405,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bKy",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 849135356,
      "version": 478,
      "versionNonce": 1765172348,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731912162737,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let's understand everyting one by one:\n\nI).What does it mean to say React.js is a library?\n->Well in our backend part we used express.js which has it's ceratin\nrule to serve file :like to send a file from server we should provide \nabsoulte path so express.js is framework built on top of js but \nReact.js is library :so what is the difference b/w \nlibrary and framework\n",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let's understand everyting one by one:\n\nI).What does it mean to say React.js is a library?\n->Well in our backend part we used express.js which has it's ceratin\nrule to serve file :like to send a file from server we should provide \nabsoulte path so express.js is framework built on top of js but \nReact.js is library :so what is the difference b/w \nlibrary and framework\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TjL8LkS8S5fcom3LYUnea",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 302.7563744911486,
      "y": 1156.1352673580245,
      "width": 1108.7996826171875,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bKz",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1433986044,
      "version": 14,
      "versionNonce": 1755072964,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731911645110,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Library\nA library is a collection of pre-written code that developers can use \nto optimize tasks. It provides functions and methods that you can \ncall to perform various operations, but the flow of control remains \nwith the developer.\n\nReact is a classic example of a library. It provides tools to create \nUI components, but you decide when and how to use those tools. \nYou have the flexibility to structure your application as you like, and \nyou call React's functions as needed.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Library\nA library is a collection of pre-written code that developers can use \nto optimize tasks. It provides functions and methods that you can \ncall to perform various operations, but the flow of control remains \nwith the developer.\n\nReact is a classic example of a library. It provides tools to create \nUI components, but you decide when and how to use those tools. \nYou have the flexibility to structure your application as you like, and \nyou call React's functions as needed.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "LpMc_N4nxMPg0_AB9GciW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 302.75634712244266,
      "y": 1537.206610957931,
      "width": 715,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bL0",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 110549372,
      "version": 84,
      "versionNonce": 703608316,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731911647909,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Characteristics of a Library:\n\n1.Focus: Solves specific problems or a set of related problems.\n\n2.Control: The developer controls the flow of the application.\n\n3.Flexibility: More flexible; you decide how and where to use it.\n\n4.Example: React, Lodash, jQuery.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Characteristics of a Library:\n\n1.Focus: Solves specific problems or a set of related problems.\n\n2.Control: The developer controls the flow of the application.\n\n3.Flexibility: More flexible; you decide how and where to use it.\n\n4.Example: React, Lodash, jQuery.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "ceWRc_RULOxbtQU1-aDQk",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 292.77635894728314,
      "y": 1922.0576708268966,
      "width": 1601.5994873046875,
      "height": 385,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bL1",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 738573436,
      "version": 106,
      "versionNonce": 1920163012,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731911826746,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Framework\nA framework, on the other hand, is a comprehensive set of tools and conventions designed to \nprovide a structured approach to software development. It dictates the architecture and flow of control \nof the application, which you follow by integrating your code into predefined structures and hooks.\n\nExpress is a good example of a framework. It provides a robust structure for building web applications \nand APIs. Express dictates the flow of control: how requests and responses are handled\nvia pre define method and route handler which have perticular set of rule , \nhow middleware is used, and how routes are defined. \nYou build your application within this framework, \nfollowing its conventions",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Framework\nA framework, on the other hand, is a comprehensive set of tools and conventions designed to \nprovide a structured approach to software development. It dictates the architecture and flow of control \nof the application, which you follow by integrating your code into predefined structures and hooks.\n\nExpress is a good example of a framework. It provides a robust structure for building web applications \nand APIs. Express dictates the flow of control: how requests and responses are handled\nvia pre define method and route handler which have perticular set of rule , \nhow middleware is used, and how routes are defined. \nYou build your application within this framework, \nfollowing its conventions",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Ir8fcIGQFIlFq9SSCIeWW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 291.11309661923826,
      "y": 2338.374910741148,
      "width": 902,
      "height": 250,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bL2",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2064513988,
      "version": 59,
      "versionNonce": 648955460,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731912045611,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Characteristics of a Framework:\n\n1.Focus: Provides a complete solution for building a specific type of application.\n\n2.Control: The framework controls the flow of the application. \nThe developer integrates their code within the framework's structure.\n\n3.Structure: Enforces a particular architecture and design patterns.\n\n4.Example: Express, Angular, Django",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Characteristics of a Framework:\n\n1.Focus: Provides a complete solution for building a specific type of application.\n\n2.Control: The framework controls the flow of the application. \nThe developer integrates their code within the framework's structure.\n\n3.Structure: Enforces a particular architecture and design patterns.\n\n4.Example: Express, Angular, Django",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "TpdqF8J53STZ93KZVKmM0",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 293.44683706146134,
      "y": 2650.2213937737997,
      "width": 1527.9612038624362,
      "height": 315,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bL3",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 170680572,
      "version": 315,
      "versionNonce": 1649877956,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731912151113,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Key Differences\na).Inversion of Control: In a library, you call the functions you need (you are in control). In a\nframework, the framework calls your code at specific points (inversion of control).\n\nb).Scope: Libraries typically provide utilities to solve specific problems. Frameworks offer a\ncomplete solution and dictate the structure of your application.\n\nc).Flexibility vs. Structure: Libraries offer more flexibility and fewer conventions. Frameworks\nenforce a particular way of doing things, providing a structured approach.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Key Differences\na).Inversion of Control: In a library, you call the functions you need (you are in control). In a framework, the framework calls your code at specific points (inversion of control).\n\nb).Scope: Libraries typically provide utilities to solve specific problems. Frameworks offer a complete solution and dictate the structure of your application.\n\nc).Flexibility vs. Structure: Libraries offer more flexibility and fewer conventions. Frameworks enforce a particular way of doing things, providing a structured approach.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "Tr3T9AebrrzuhecPrPRoW",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 283.6288158504118,
      "y": 3020.178054744967,
      "width": 1601.5994873046875,
      "height": 350,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bL4",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1926378052,
      "version": 91,
      "versionNonce": 480785476,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731912154597,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Example Scenario\nImagine building a house:\n\na).Library: It's like having a toolkit. You use different tools (React components, Lodash functions) as \nneeded to build parts of your house. You decide how to use these tools.\n\nb).Framework: It's like having a pre-fabricated house structure. You follow the blueprint provided by \nthe framework (Express routes, middleware) to build your house. \nThe framework dictates how the house is constructed, but you add your custom elements within \nthis structure.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Example Scenario\nImagine building a house:\n\na).Library: It's like having a toolkit. You use different tools (React components, Lodash functions) as \nneeded to build parts of your house. You decide how to use these tools.\n\nb).Framework: It's like having a pre-fabricated house structure. You follow the blueprint provided by \nthe framework (Express routes, middleware) to build your house. \nThe framework dictates how the house is constructed, but you add your custom elements within \nthis structure.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
