    {
      "id": "id9rmEVw6tmfQhEELQUcu",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 277.30360971209495,
      "y": 20431.28283125034,
      "width": 1228.79931640625,
      "height": 360,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLK",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 951270980,
      "version": 250,
      "versionNonce": 1277971324,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731916375295,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So this was all about the difference b/w Library and \nframework ,now let's see what is react single page application\nfunctionality\n\n\n\n\nII)React-SPA(Single Page Application)",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So this was all about the difference b/w Library and \nframework ,now let's see what is react single page application\nfunctionality\n\n\n\n\nII)React-SPA(Single Page Application)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "1FVhg6ssY0JigJJQhvR2Y",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 269.1083839283963,
      "y": 20819.663352984087,
      "width": 1355.1998291015625,
      "height": 105,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLL",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1769249916,
      "version": 240,
      "versionNonce": 839047620,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731916440858,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "SO react-spa simply means that when ever a event get's triggered at that time instead \nof change/re-rendering the whole page react only render the perticular element which is \nchanged or added",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "SO react-spa simply means that when ever a event get's triggered at that time instead \nof change/re-rendering the whole page react only render the perticular element which is \nchanged or added",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "0KBeJJSDvTAx0x0tDwl3E",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 262.4244775978988,
      "y": 20953.34461197862,
      "width": 1555.3995361328125,
      "height": 140,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLM",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 206415228,
      "version": 59,
      "versionNonce": 153795012,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731916930686,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "A Single-Page Application is a web application that loads a single HTML page and dynamically updates \nthat page as the user interacts with the app. Instead of loading entire new pages from the server, \nSPAs use AJAX to fetch and render only the necessary content, leading to faster and smoother user \ninteractions",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "A Single-Page Application is a web application that loads a single HTML page and dynamically updates \nthat page as the user interacts with the app. Instead of loading entire new pages from the server, \nSPAs use AJAX to fetch and render only the necessary content, leading to faster and smoother user \ninteractions",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "nE1AxcPEnq7hytuPI-UKz",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 255.53139717374648,
      "y": 21134.022648500024,
      "width": 1632.3994140625,
      "height": 420,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLN",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 554419580,
      "version": 48,
      "versionNonce": 927026684,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731917043702,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Why Use React for SPAs?\n1.Component-Based Architecture: React's component-based architecture allows developers to build reusable, \nself-contained UI components.\n\n2.Virtual DOM: React uses a virtual DOM to efficiently update and render components, \nmaking the app fast and responsive.\n\n3.Declarative Syntax: React's declarative syntax makes it easy to manage and understand the state of \nthe application.\n\n4.Rich Ecosystem: React has a rich ecosystem of libraries and tools that make it easier to manage state, \nhandle routing, and interact with APIs.",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Why Use React for SPAs?\n1.Component-Based Architecture: React's component-based architecture allows developers to build reusable, \nself-contained UI components.\n\n2.Virtual DOM: React uses a virtual DOM to efficiently update and render components, \nmaking the app fast and responsive.\n\n3.Declarative Syntax: React's declarative syntax makes it easy to manage and understand the state of \nthe application.\n\n4.Rich Ecosystem: React has a rich ecosystem of libraries and tools that make it easier to manage state, \nhandle routing, and interact with APIs.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "5kK6Rsu-DqI0qKa_UgHTM",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 268.06394743654863,
      "y": 21678.35522813674,
      "width": 1293.599609375,
      "height": 35,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLO",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 828735172,
      "version": 108,
      "versionNonce": 1379603708,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731917081586,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Let's understand with a example and let's build a simple app to understand react-spa",
      "fontSize": 28,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Let's understand with a example and let's build a simple app to understand react-spa",
