      "updated": 1731934234684,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "So this what react-spa means",
      "fontSize": 68.1909274181991,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "So this what react-spa means ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "-Yj7hFrTykz7H8GLIfY6_",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -98.81199052000295,
      "y": 44478.809598996086,
      "width": 1265.1539882077122,
      "height": 179.70948411886275,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLq",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1104607044,
      "version": 159,
      "versionNonce": 859575932,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731934948401,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Now let's get into react as the library \n\nGetting Started with React(creating a react app)",
      "fontSize": 47.922529098363405,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Now let's get into react as the library \n\nGetting Started with React(creating a react app)",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "NXk6895xKClzk-D_DmwvP",
      "type": "text",
      "x": -90.98785900443568,
      "y": 44684.47323668767,
      "width": 2059.19873046875,
      "height": 540,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bLr",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2061700988,
      "version": 11,
      "versionNonce": 99250500,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1731934939277,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "1. What is React?\nReact is a popular JavaScript library for building user interfaces, \nparticularly single-page applications where you can navigate between different views without \nrefreshing the entire page. It was developed by Facebook and is maintained by a community of developers.\n\nKey Concepts:\n\n1.Component-Based: React encourages you to build your user interface using reusable components.\n\n2.Declarative: React makes it easy to describe what the UI should look like for any given state.\n\n3.Learn Once, Write Anywhere: You can use React to build web, mobile, and desktop applications.",
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 8,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1. What is React?\nReact is a popular JavaScript library for building user interfaces, \nparticularly single-page applications where you can navigate between different views without \nrefreshing the entire page. It was developed by Facebook and is maintained by a community of developers.\n\nKey Concepts:\n\n1.Component-Based: React encourages you to build your user interface using reusable components.\n\n2.Declarative: React makes it easy to describe what the UI should look like for any given state.\n\n3.Learn Once, Write Anywhere: You can use React to build web, mobile, and desktop applications.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "E3x9wtpY_uAXD_I0vVMvR",
      "type": "line",
      "x": -110.82770294506031,
      "y": 44654.294389974806,
      "width": 1353.5801783426502,
      "height": 2.2354661473000306,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
